<p>In the latest development in the Israel-Iran conflict, President Trump said U.S. combat operations against Iran are continuing “in full force” and will proceed until Washington’s “objectives are achieved.” He acknowledged the deaths of three U.S. service members and warned that more U.S. casualties are likely. Trump said the U.S. would “avenge” the Americans killed and asked for prayers for five others he said were seriously wounded. Trump defended the campaign by arguing that Iran was on the verge of obtaining nuclear weapons, a claim at least one outlet said has been debunked.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/QRixYaSllB6LPyo983NN6xygW9toWpSGtL2s11HTMlrJku0u3QaX2a3TcOqG9brsDBapCxhRN5JJ2PlarabiMW1a3l-M5dAcSk9VK-FoEEtnQHgrwP28UTD8i2wJeQX973ICu-t6Ltl2_AJqXSVEst0DHnVZ1JwA1WrR1wgdMx43TZeFbucnbl15Zfj2c-U' alt='President Trump delivers remarks as coverage focuses on the continuing U.S.-Israel campaign against Iran.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Joint-campaign framing: Some outlets described the operation as a joint U.S.-Israeli strike campaign against Iran.</li><li>Scale framing: One report said Trump cast Washington’s offensive as one of the largest in modern history.</li><li>Diplomatic backdrop: Al Jazeera noted Trump’s vow to keep attacking came even after he had floated diplomatic off-ramps.</li><li>Format detail: Firstpost described the update as a roughly six-minute video message posted on social media.</li></ul><blockquote>Combat operations continue at this time in full force, and they will continue until all of our objectives are achieved. - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Donald Trump: He called the campaign a “righteous mission,” accused Iran’s leadership of “waging war against civilization itself,” and said strikes will continue until the U.S. meets its objectives. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/trump-says-combat-operations-iran-will-continue-until-all-objectives-achieved'>Al-Monitor (Reuters)</a>, <a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/mar/01/trump-more-deaths-military-iran'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Pentagon / US Central Command: The Pentagon confirmed three American deaths in the conflict. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/us/diplomacy/article/3345054/pentagon-confirms-three-american-deaths-iran-war'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>The Guardian: The paper reported that Trump cited claims that Iran was on the verge of getting nuclear weapons and said those claims have been debunked. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/mar/01/trump-more-deaths-military-iran'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-video-address-iran-israel-combat-operations-continue-until-objectives-achieved/'>Trump says operations will &quot;continue until all of our objectives are achieved&quot;</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/3/2/trump-says-likely-more-us-casualties-attacks-on-iran-will-continue'>Trump says likely more US casualties, attacks on Iran will continue</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/trump-says-combat-operations-iran-will-continue-until-all-objectives-achieved'>Trump says combat operations in Iran will continue until all objectives achieved</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/us-israel-strikes-on-iran-west-asia-conflict-trump-death-toll-american-troops-war-end-13985165.html'>Trump warns death toll of US troops &#x27;likely to increase&#x27;, says US, Israel strikes on Iran might last 4 weeks</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/trump-says-there-will-likely-be-more-us-service-members-killed-in-israel-iran-conflict-before-it-ends/article70693003.ece'>Trump says ‘there will likely be more’ U.S. service members killed in Israel-Iran conflict before it ends</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://w